rules:[
 ['Buildings are places at real size.',' A wizard is 0.9 u across and 1.8 m tall, so 1 u is about 0.6 m and a metre of height is about 14.5 art px. An academy range is 40 to 60 m long (60 to 90 u); three storeys fill most of a screen.'],
 ['Tall buildings stand on the far sides.',' North or west on a plan rises off the top of the screen without hiding play. Anything south or east stays low (a wall, a hedge), or would have to fade.'],
 ['The camera sees a facade\'s foot.',' From 4 u away you see about 6 m of a wall, from 12 u only its base, so the ground floor carries the art (doors, windows, buttresses, steps), and lessons that should feel like the academy run along the buildings.'],
 ['Every map is bigger than a screen,',' at least 1.5 screens in the direction you travel.'],
 ['What you can see depends on the direction.',' From your wizard the view reaches 7.6 units straight down the screen, 13.6 straight up, 15 sideways, and 17 to 20 into the corners. Plans are turned 45 degrees, so north or west on a plan heads for an upper corner, with about 19 units visible. South or east shows about 11.'],
 ['You see enemies coming.',' A fight wants at least 15 units of visible approach, so enemies should arrive from the north or west of a plan.'],
 ['Four wizards fit.',' A Fire ring is 3 units in radius, so a fight wants about 6 units per player, and a room at least 24 by 18.'],
 ['Walks vary, and some are long.',' Sometimes you walk a while before anything happens, because that makes the world feel real. You cross a screen in about 7 seconds.'],
],
